# Build context filter for the WEB image specifically.
#
# BuildKit looks for `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` before falling back to the context root's
# `.dockerignore` — so this file shadows the root one for `docker build -f apps/web/Dockerfile`.
# It has to exist: the root `.dockerignore` excludes `apps/web` outright (correct for the API image,
# which has no use for the frontend and benefits from the smaller context), which stripped the web
# app out of its own build. Caught by the CI image job on its first green run of the API image.
#
# Patterns are relative to the CONTEXT root (the repo root), not to this directory.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
.git
.github
**/*.log
**/coverage
.env
.env.*
docs
*.md
